ed, 0.8436) and the earlier RF (0.83), LogFare/wt/Deck/AgeBin variants (≤0.8436).\n\nValidation evidence (executed): The evaluator measured the fixed-split accuracy; the best reported is 0.8492 for the LR+ExtraTrees soft-vote. Single-factor results measured along the way: majority floor ~0.615, sex-only ~0.776, baseline LR ~0.816, +Title/FamilySize/IsAlone ~0.8436, RF ~0.832, LogFare ~0.832, class_weight ~0.827.\n\nChanges from parent: started from an LR baseline using raw Pclass/SibSp/Parch/Sex/Embarked with Age/Fare imputation. Added Name-derived Title, FamilySize, IsAlone, standardized numerics, and finally a soft-voting ExtraTrees ensemble.\n\nArtifacts: predictions.csv (418 rows, PassengerId+Survived, test order), work/val_predictions.csv (179 rows aligned to validation.csv), work/model_blend_et.joblib (dict {"lr","et"}), work/metrics.json, work/README.txt. Earlier single-model artifacts retained: work/model_final.joblib.\n\nLoad: joblib.load("work/model_blend_et.joblib"); prob = 0.5*lr.predict_proba(X)[:,1] + 0.5*et.predict_proba(X)[:,1]; Survived = (prob>=0.5).astype(int). Apply the same featurize() to raw rows before predict.\n</description>\n<code>\n# featurize(df): add FamilySize, IsAlone, Title (Name regex; Mlle/Ms->Miss, Mme->Mrs, rare->Rare)\n# ColumnTransformer:\n#   num = SimpleImputer(median)+StandardScaler on [Pclass,SibSp,Parch,FamilySize,IsAlone]\n#   af  = SimpleImputer(median, add_indicator=True)+StandardScaler on [Age,Fare]\n#   cat = SimpleImputer(constant \'M\')+OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\'ignore\') on [Sex,Embarked,Title]\n# lr = Pipeline(pre, LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, random_state=42)).fit(X_tr,y_tr)\n# et = Pipeline(pre, ExtraTreesClassifier(n_estimators=400, max_depth=6, min_samples_leaf=4,\n#                                         random_state=42, n_jobs=4)).fit(X_tr,y_tr)\n# prob = 0.5*lr.predict_proba(X)[:,1] + 0.5*et.predict_proba(X)[:,1]\n# Survived = (prob>=0.5).astype(int)\n# val -> work/val_predictions.csv (aligned to validation.csv PassengerId order)\n# test -> predictions.csv (418 rows, header PassengerId,Survived, no index)\n# joblib.dump({"lr":lr,"et":et}, "work/model_blend_et.joblib")\n</code>\n<suggestions>\nObserved weaknesses (evidence): The validation set is only 179 rows, so single-trial accuracy swings by ~1–2 points are within noise; the 0.8436→0.8492 gain from the ensemble is plausible but small and could partly be noise. RF, LogFare, class_weight, C-tuning, Deck and AgeBin added no gain; LR on the chosen features is a strong, stable baseline.\n\nLessons (evidence): (1) The validation set is supplied pre-split; do not re-split the 712-row train file (caused the 143-vs-179 failure). (2) Scaling numerics removed lbfgs convergence warnings without changing accuracy. (3) Tree ensembles only helped as a soft complement to LR (LR+ExtraTrees), not standalone (RF/GB regressed).\n\nPrioritized next experiments (hypotheses, not yet run): (1) Re-tune ExtraTrees depth/leaf and the LR/ET blend weight (0.5 fixed here) via internal 5-fold CV on the 712 train rows — test whether the blend weight and leaf size matter beyond noise. (2) Add a small calibrated HistGradientBoosting as a third voter with weight chosen by CV; verify it beats the two-model blend on the fixed 179-row validation. (3) Calibrate probabilities (Platt/isotonic on internal CV) to check if threshold 0.5 remains optimal for accuracy. (4) Confirm run-to-run stability by varying the ET n_jobs/seed-free components; keep seed 42 and report variance across internal CV folds rather than trusting a single fixed-split number.\n</suggestions>', role='assistant', tool_calls=None, function_call=None, provider_specific_fields=None), provider_specific_fields={})], usage=Usage(completion_tokens=1435, prompt_tokens=30829, total_tokens=32264, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=PromptTokensDetailsWrapper(audio_tokens=None, cache_write_tokens=None, cached_tokens=28672, image_tokens=None, text_tokens=None), prompt_c