es.\n\nFeature handling (identical to parent, fit-safe): featurize(df) adds FamilySize=SibSp+Parch+1, IsAlone=(FamilySize==1), Title from Name regex ", ([^.]+)." mapping Mlle/Ms→Miss, Mme→Mrs, rare (count<10 over training rows)→Rare, encoded as a fitted mapping. Preprocessing is one shared ColumnTransformer fit on training rows only: StandardScaler on [Pclass,SibSp,Parch,FamilySize,IsAlone]; SimpleImputer(median, add_indicator=True)+StandardScaler on [Age,Fare]; SimpleImputer(constant \'M\')+OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\'ignore\') on [Sex,Embarked,Title].\n\nModels: LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, random_state=42) and ExtraTreesClassifier(n_estimators=400, random_state=42, n_jobs=4). Soft-vote probability w*LR + (1-w)*ET; Survived = prob>=0.5. Device CPU; seed 42; n_jobs≤4.\n\nSearch plan (CV-selected, then single validation evaluation):\n- Reuse the parent\'s winning LR C by refitting LR on all 712 rows; ET depth/leaf and blend weight swept together.\n- Grid: blend weight w ∈ {0.4,0.5,0.6,0.7}; ET max_depth ∈ {5,6,7,8}; min_samples_leaf ∈ {2,3,4,6}. That is 4*4*4=64 combos total but per family ≤16; evaluate each of the 4 weights against each of the 16 ET settings on the same CV splits, then report top-3 by mean CV accuracy.\n- Selection metric: mean 5-fold StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42) accuracy of the blend computed with out-of-fold probabilities.\n- Procedures must be nested: fit preprocessing inside each fold (or fit on full training set before CV — do the latter for speed, documented as a minor optimistic bias). Chosen configuration is fit on all 712 rows.\n- Evaluate the single CV-chosen configuration exactly once on the fixed 179-row validation. Accept only if strictly greater than the incumbent 0.8492; otherwise fall back to the parent\'s fixed 0.5 / max_depth 6 / min_samples_leaf 4.\n\nBudget: 64 combos × 5 folds × (LR + ExtraTrees 400 trees) ≈ under 3 min on 8-core CPU with n_jobs=4; cap CV folds at 5 and reuse identical fold indices across combos.\n\nOutputs (same format as parent):\n- predictions.csv in working dir: header exactly PassengerId,Survived, 418 rows, test order preserved, integers 0/1, no index.\n- work/val_predictions.csv: 179 rows PassengerId,Survived aligned to validation.csv order (same winning model).\n- work/metrics.json: fixed-validation accuracy, CV mean±std of chosen vs incumbent, sweep table.\n- work/model_blend_best.joblib: dict {"lr","et","w"} compatible with parent\'s loader (parent used w=0.5 fixed; here store w).\n- work/sweep_comparison.csv and work/README.txt stating proba>=0.5→1 and both val/test predictions come from the same winning model.\n- Print a short table of CV mean accuracy per combo and the validation accuracy for the CV-winning combo vs incumbent 0.8492.</experiment>\n<code_outline>import os, json, joblib, numpy as np, pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\nfrom sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, OneHotEncoder\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import ExtraTreesClassifier\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedKFold\nfrom sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score\n\nSEED = 42; WARD = \'work\'; os.makedirs(WARD, exist_ok=True)\ntr = pd.read_csv(\'../input/data/train_data/train.csv\')\nva = pd.read_csv(\'../input/data/validation_data/validation.csv\')\nte = pd.read_csv(\'../input/data/predict_data/test.csv\')\n\n# protocol: fixed validation IDs\nval_ids_path = f\'{WARD}/val_ids.json\'\nif os.path.exists(val_ids_path):\n    assert json.load(open(val_ids_path)) == va[\'PassengerId\'].tolist(), \'val IDs changed\'\nelse:\n    json.dump(va[\'PassengerId\'].tolist(), open(val_ids_path, \'w\'))\nassert not set(tr[\'PassengerId\']) & set(va[\'PassengerId\'])\nassert not set(tr[\'PassengerId\']) & set(te[\'PassengerId\'])\nassert not set(va[\'PassengerId\']) & set(te[\'PassengerId\'])\n\ndef featurize(df):\n    d = df.copy()\n    d[\'FamilySize\'] = d[\'SibSp\'] + d[\'Parch\'] + 1\n    d[\'IsAlone\'] = (d[\'FamilySize\'] == 1).astype(int)\n    def title(n):\n        t = n.split(\',\')[1].split(\'.\')[0].strip()\n        if t in (\'Mlle\', \'Ms\'): return \'Miss\'\n        if t == \'Mme\': return \'Mrs\'\n        return t\n    d[\'Title\'] = d[\'Name\'].map(title)\n    return d\n\ntr_f, va_f, te_f = featurize(tr), featurize(va), featurize(te)\ntitle_counts = tr_f[\'Title\'].value_counts()\nrare = title_counts[title_counts < 10].index\nfor d in (tr_f, va_f, te_f):\n    d[\'Title\'] = d[\'Title\'].where(~d[\'Title\'].isin(rare), \'Rare\')\ntr_f[\'Embarked\'] = tr_f[\'Embarked\'].fillna(\'M\'); va_f[\'Embarked\'] = va_f[\'Embarked\'].fillna(\'M\'); te_f[\'Embarked\'] = te_f[\'Embarked\'].fillna(\'M\')\n\nnum = [\'Pclass\', \'SibSp\', \'Parch\', \'FamilySize\', \'IsAlone\']\naf = [\'Age\', \'Fare\']\ncat = [\'Sex\', \'Embarked\', \'Title\']\npre = ColumnTransformer([\n    (\'num\', StandardScaler(), num),\n    (\'af\', Pipeline([(\'imp\', SimpleImputer(strategy=\'median\', add_indicator=True)),\n                     (\'sc\', StandardScaler())]), af),\n    (\'cat\', Pipeline([(\'imp\', SimpleImputer(strategy=\'constant\', fill_value=\'M\')),\n                      (\'oh\', OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\'ignore\'))]), cat),\n])\n\ndef fit_models(X, y, depth, leaf):\n    lr = Pipeline([(\'pre\', pre), (\'lr\', LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, random_state=SEED))]).fit(X, y)\n    et = Pipeline([(\'pre\', pre), (\'et\', ExtraTreesClassifier(\n        n_estimators=400, max_depth=depth, min_samples_leaf=leaf, random_state=SEED, n_jobs=4))]).fit(X, y)\n    return lr, et\n\ny = tr_f[\'Survived\'].values\nX = tr_f.drop(columns=[\'Survived\'])\nskf = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=SEED)\nfolds = list(skf.split(X, y))\n\nresults = []\nfor depth in [5, 6, 7, 8]:\n    for leaf in [2, 3, 4, 6]:\n        oof_lr = np.zeros(len(y)); oof_et = np.zeros(len(y))\n        for tr_idx, va_idx in folds:\n            lr, et = fit_models(X.iloc[tr_idx], y[tr_idx], depth, leaf)\n            oof_lr[va_idx] = lr.predict_proba(X.iloc[va_idx])[:, 1]\n            oof_et[va_idx] = et.predict_proba(X.iloc[va_idx])[:, 1]\n        for w in [0.4, 0.5, 0.6, 0.7]:\n            prob = w * oof_lr + (1 - w) * oof_et\n            acc = accuracy_score(y, (prob >= 0.5).astype(int))\n            results.append(dict(w=w, depth=depth, leaf=leaf, cv_acc=acc))\nres = pd.DataFrame(results).sort_values(\'cv_acc\', ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\nres.to_csv(f\'{WARD}/sweep_comparison.csv\', index=False)\nbest = res.iloc[0]\nprint(res.head(10).to_string())\n\n# fit final CV-chosen config on all 712 training rows\nlr, et = fit_models(X, y, int(best.depth), int(best.leaf))\nXv = va_f.reindex(columns=X.columns)\nprob_v = best.w * lr.predict_proba(Xv)[:, 1] + (1 - best.w) * et.predict_proba(Xv)[:, 1]\nval_pred = (prob_v >= 0.5).astype(int)\n# Note: report val accuracy here only if evaluator is available; per protocol do NOT read validation labels.\n# We write predictions; the evaluator will score them. We record the CV number for the chosen config.\nmetrics = {\'cv_mean\': float(best.cv_acc), \'chosen\': {\'w\': float(best.w), \'depth\': int(best.depth), \'leaf\': int(best.leaf)},\n           \'incumbent_val_accuracy\': 0.8492, \'note\': \'fixed-validation accuracy measured by evaluator\'}\njson.dump(metrics, open(f\'{WARD}/metrics.json\', \'w\'), indent=2)\n\npd.DataFrame({\'PassengerId\': va[\'PassengerId\'], \'Survived\': val_pred}).to_csv(f\'{WARD}/val_predictions.csv\', index=False)\n\nXt = te_f.reindex(columns=X.columns)\nprob_t = best.w * lr.predict_proba(Xt)[:, 1] + (1 - best.w) * et.predict_proba(Xt)[:, 1]\ntest_pred = (prob_t >= 0.5).astype(int)\npd.DataFrame({\'PassengerId\': te[\'PassengerId\'], \'Survived\': test_pred}).to_csv(\'predictions.csv\', index=False)\nassert len(test_pred) == 418 and set(np.unique(test_pred)).issubset({0, 1})\n\njoblib.dump({\'lr\': lr, \'et\': et, \'w\': float(best.w)}, f\'{WARD}/model_blend_best.joblib\')\nwith open(f\'{WARD}/README.txt\', \'w\') as f:\n    f.write(\'prob >= 0.5 -> 1; validation and test predictions from the same CV-tuned LR+ET blend.\\n\')\nprint(\'wrote predictions.csv and work/val_predictions.csv\')</code_outline>\n\nRead local data from ../input/data/. It contains the fixed public training split,\nunlabeled validation inputs in validation_data/, a sample validation prediction\nfile and the unlabeled business prediction data. Inspect their actual schemas.\n<data_preview>```\ninput/\n    data/\n        validation_sample_predictions.csv (180 lines)\n        validation_schema.json (64 lines)\n        predict_data/\n            test.csv (419 lines)\n        train_data/\n            train.csv (713 lines)\n        validation_data/\n            validation.csv (180 lines)\nworking/\n    best_code.py (114 lines)\n    coder.log (1469 lines)\n    experiment.json (7 lines)\n    llm.log (84 lines)\n    predictions.csv (419 lines)\n    best_prediction/\n        predictions.csv (419 lines)\n    work/\n        README.txt (1 lines)\n        metrics.json (4 lines)\n        model_agebin.joblib (6.2 kB)\n        model_baseline.joblib (4.6 kB)\n        model_best.joblib (5.9 kB)\n        model_blend.joblib (273.8 kB)\n        model_blend_et.joblib (1.9 MB)\n        model_cw.joblib (5.0 kB)\n        ... and 6 other files```</data_preview>\n\nThe business task defines the target, primary metric, validation strategy, output\ncolumns, row identifiers and constraints. Use only supplied local data and parent\nartifacts. Do not download datasets, pretrained weights or predictions. Fit all\npreprocessing on training rows only; never read hidden validation labels, source\ntraining files outside ../input/data/, or the private evaluator workspace.\nThe validation split is fixed for all experiments; do not change it to improve scores.\nYou may create an internal training holdout for tuning without changing the fixed\nexternal validation inputs. Record seeds and avoid target leakage.\n\nStart with a working baseline, then change a small number of factors at a time.\nUse observed execution errors and measured validation scores to choose improvements.\nExplain gains and regressions; do not claim results that were not executed.\nWrite complete prediction outputs for both validation and the business prediction\nset in the same cell. The business output must be ./predictions.csv and\nmust preserve the task\'s identifiers, ordering and schema. Save model, preprocessing\nand inference instructions in the working directory as requested by the task.\nParent artifacts, when supplied, are copied into ./ and can be reused; outputs\nfrom other workers in the current round are unavailable. Check alignment before\ncombining any predictions from your own local experiments.\nParent files may include later trials: check checkpoint metadata against the\nparent\'s scored code before reuse; retrain if their provenance is uncertain.\n\nA persistent Jupyter session is used. Propose one cell at a time, inspect its output,\nrepair failures, and then refine the best measured method within the budget.\nCheck package availability before use; use packages installed in this environment.\n<execution_environment>\nLocal execution platform: Darwin; CPU logical cores: 8.\nSelected training device: cpu.\nUse CPU training. Do not require CUDA, NVIDIA tools, or an MPS accelerator.\nIn notebook code, os.environ[\'BIZMIND_DEVICE\'] identifies the selected backend. Respect CPU limits and scale batch/model sizes to available memory; no GPU memory reservation is provided.\nCPU core limit: 4; keep n_jobs and thread counts within it.\nMaximum time per code cell: 3600 seconds.\n</execution_environment>\nUse torch.device(os.environ[\'BIZMIND_DEVICE\']) for PyTorch models and tensors.\nDo not hardcode .cuda(). On MPS/CPU do not require CUDA-only operations or packages.\nUse CPU for libraries without support for the detected accelerator and choose\nmodel and batch sizes that fit available memory.\n\n<completed_local_parent_code>import os, json, joblib, numpy as np, pandas as pd, warnings\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\nfrom sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\nwarnings.filterwarnings("ignore")\n\nseed = 42\nbase = "../input/data"\ntrain = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/train_data/train.csv")\nval = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/validation_data/validation.csv")\ntest = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/predict_data/test.csv")\n\ndef featurize(df):\n    d = df.copy()\n    d["FamilySize"] = d["SibSp"] + d["Parch"] + 1\n    d["IsAlone"] = (d["FamilySize"] == 1).astype(int)\n    title = d["Name"].str.extract(r",\\s*([^.]+)\\.", expand=False)\n    title = title.replace({"Mlle":"Miss","Ms":"Miss","Mme":"Mrs"})\n    rare = ~title.isin(["Mr","Mrs","Miss","Master"])\n    d["Title"] = np.where(rare, "Rare", title.fillna("Rare"))\n    return d\n\ntr_f, val_f, te_f = featurize(train), featurize(val), featurize(test)\nX_tr = tr_f.drop(columns=["Survived"]); y_tr = tr_f["Survived"].values\nval_ids = val_f["PassengerId"].tolist()\n\nnum_cols = ["Pclass", "SibSp", "Parch", "FamilySize", "IsAlone"]\naf_cols = ["Age", "Fare"]\ncat_cols = ["Sex", "Embarked", "Title"]\n\npre = ColumnTransformer([\n    ("num", Pipeline([("imp", SimpleImputer(strategy="median")), ("sc", StandardScaler())]), num_cols),\n    ("af", Pipeline([("imp", SimpleImputer(strategy="median", add_indicator=True)), ("sc", StandardScaler())]), af_cols),\n    ("cat", Pipeline([("imp", SimpleImputer(strategy="constant", fill_value="M")),\n                      ("oh", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown="ignore"))]), cat_cols),\n])\nclf = Pipeline([("pre", pre), ("lr", LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, random_state=seed))])\nclf.fit(X_tr, y_tr)\n\nval_prob = clf.predict_proba(val_f)[:, 1]\nval_pred = (val_prob >= 0.5).astype(int)\npd.DataFrame({"PassengerId": val_ids, "Survived": val_pred}).to_csv(\n    "work/val_predictions.csv", index=False)\n\ntest_pred = (clf.predict_proba(te_f)[:, 1] >= 0.5).astype(int)\npp = pd.DataFrame({"PassengerId": te_f["PassengerId"].values, "Survived": test_pred})\npp.to_csv("predictions.csv", index=False)\n\njson.dump({"model": "LR + Title/FamilySize/IsAlone (final best)",\n           "seed": seed,\n           "features_numeric": num_cols,\n           "features_agefare": af_cols,\n           "features_cat": cat_cols,\n           "note": "best measured fixed-split validation accuracy across trials"},\n          open("work/metrics.json", "w"), indent=2)\njoblib.dump(clf, "work/model_final.joblib")\nopen("work/README.txt", "w").write(\n    "FINAL INFERENCE NOTE\\n"\n    "Model: LogisticRegression on engineered Titanic features.\\n"\n    "Load work/model_final.joblib; predict_proba[:,1] >= 0.5 -> Survived=1 else 0.\\n"\n    "Features: scaled Pclass,SibSp,Parch,FamilySize(=SibSp+Parch+1),IsAlone; "\n    "Age & Fare median-imputed with missing indicators then scaled; "\n    "Sex, Embarked (missing->\'M\'), Title (Mr/Mrs/Miss/Master/rare->Rare) one-hot.\\n"\n    "Trained on all 712 rows of train_data/train.csv. Validation = 179 rows of "\n    "validation_data/validation.csv aligned by PassengerId. Seed 42, CPU only.\\n"\n    "Deliverables: predictions.csv (418 rows, PassengerId+Survived), "\n    "work/val_predictions.csv (179 rows).")\n\nvp = pd.read_csv("work/val_predictions.csv")\nassert vp["PassengerId"].tolist() == val_ids and len(vp) == 179\nassert list(vp.columns) == ["PassengerId", "Survived"]\nassert len(pp) == 418 and list(pp.columns) == ["PassengerId", "Survived"]\nassert pp["PassengerId"].tolist() == te_f["PassengerId"].tolist()\nassert set(pp["Survived"].unique()) <= {0, 1} and pp["Survived"].dtype.kind in "iu"\nprint("FINAL val rows", len(vp), "test rows", len(pp),\n      "val pos rate", vp["Survived"].mean().round(3),\n      "test pos rate", pp["Survived"].mean().round(3))\nprint(open("work/README.txt").read())\n\nclf = joblib.load("work/model_final.joblib")\n\ndef featurize(df):\n    d = df.copy()\n    d["FamilySize"] = d["SibSp"] + d["Parch"] + 1\n    d["IsAlone"] = (d["FamilySize"] == 1).astype(int)\n    title = d["Name"].str.extract(r",\\s*([^.]+)\\.", expand=False)\n    title = title.replace({"Mlle":"Miss","Ms":"Miss","Mme":"Mrs"})\n    rare = ~title.isin(["Mr","Mrs","Miss","Master"])\n    d["Title"] = np.where(rare, "Rare", title.fillna("Rare"))\n    return d\n\n_re_val = (clf.predict_proba(featurize(val))[:, 1] >= 0.5).astype(int)\n_re_test = (clf.predict_proba(featurize(test))[:, 1] >= 0.5).astype(int)\n\nvp = pd.read_csv("work/val_predictions.csv")\npp = pd.read_csv("predictions.csv")\n\n# schema + alignment checks\nassert list(vp.columns) == ["PassengerId", "Survived"] and len(vp) == 179\nassert list(pp.columns) == ["PassengerId", "Survived"] and len(pp) == 418\nassert vp["PassengerId"].tolist() == val["PassengerId"].tolist()\nassert pp["PassengerId"].tolist() == test["PassengerId"].tolist()\nassert set(vp["Survived"].unique()) <= {0,1} and set(pp["Survived"].unique()) <= {0,1}\n\n# reproducibility: saved files equal fresh reload predictions\nassert (vp["Survived"].values == _re_val).all(), "val drift"\nassert (pp["Survived"].values == _re_test).all(), "test drift"\n\nprint("Reproducibility OK. Saved predictions match reloaded model.")\nprint("val rows", len(vp), "| test rows", len(pp))\nprint("metrics.json:\\n", open("work/metrics.json").read())\nprint("Deliverables confirmed: predictions.csv + work/val_predictions.csv")</completed_local_parent_code>\n\nRespond with exactly one executable notebook cell, using these tags:\n<goal>Hypothesis, expected runtime, expected output and how it tests the hypothesis</goal>\n<code>Python code for the next cell, without Markdown fences</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>Relative file path for complete validation predictions, or None</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>Relative file path for complete business prediction output, or None</prediction_file>\nBoth file tags must be None unless this cell writes BOTH complete outputs.\nDo not report an estimated score: the independent local evaluator measures it.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '<goal>Run the round-4 CV sweep over blend weight w, ExtraTrees max_depth and min_samples_leaf on the 712 training rows only, pick the best by 5-fold OOF accuracy, fit it on all 712 rows, and write both validation and test predictions (prob>=0.5->1) from that single winning model. Expected runtime ~2-3 min on 4 cores. Output: CV sweep table, val/test prediction files, metrics.json, sweep_comparison.csv, model_blend_best.joblib, README.txt. Tests the hypothesis that a CV-tuned blend beats the incumbent 0.8492; falls back to the incumbent 0.5/6/4 if no CV gain is found.</goal>\n<code>import os, json, joblib, warnings, time\nimport numpy as np, pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, OneHotEncoder\nfrom sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import ExtraTreesClassifier\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedKFold\nfrom sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score\nwarnings.filterwarnings("ignore")\n\nSEED = 42\nWARD = "work"; os.makedirs(WARD, exist_ok=True)\nbase = "../input/data"\ntrain = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/train_data/train.csv")\nval   = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/validation_data/validation.csv")\ntest  = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/predict_data/test.csv")\n\n# ---- protocol: fixed validation IDs ----\nval_ids_path = f"{WARD}/val_ids.json"\nval_ids = val["PassengerId"].tolist()\nif os.path.exists(val_ids_path):\n    assert json.load(open(val_ids_path)) == val_ids, "val IDs changed"\nelse:\n    json.dump(val_ids, open(val_ids_path, "w"))\nassert not set(train["PassengerId"]) & set(val["PassengerId"])\nassert not set(train["PassengerId"]) & set(test["PassengerId"])\nassert not set(val["PassengerId"]) & set(test["PassengerId"])\n\ndef featurize(df):\n    d = df.copy()\n    d["FamilySize"] = d["SibSp"] + d["Parch"] + 1\n    d["IsAlone"] = (d["FamilySize"] == 1).astype(int)\n    title = d["Name"].str.extract(r",\\s*([^.]+)\\.", expand=False)\n    title = title.replace({"Mlle": "Miss", "Ms": "Miss", "Mme": "Mrs"})\n    d["Title"] = title.fillna("Rare")\n    return d\n\ntr_f, val_f, te_f = featurize(train), featurize(val), featurize(test)\n# rare titles (count<10 over training rows) -> \'Rare\' using fitted mapping\ntc = tr_f["Title"].value_counts()\nrare = tc[tc < 10].index\nfor d in (tr_f, val_f, te_f):\n    d["Title"] = d["Title"].where(~d["Title"].isin(rare), "Rare")\nfor d in (tr_f, val_f, te_f):\n    d["Embarked"] = d["Embarked"].fillna("M")\n\nnum_cols = ["Pclass", "SibSp", "Parch", "FamilySize", "IsAlone"]\naf_cols  = ["Age", "Fare"]\ncat_cols = ["Sex", "Embarked", "Title"]\n\ndef make_pre():\n    return ColumnTransformer([\n        ("num", Pipeline([("imp", SimpleImputer(strategy="median")), ("sc", StandardScaler())]), num_cols),\n        ("af",  Pipeline([("imp", SimpleImputer(strategy="median", add_indicator=True)), ("sc", StandardScaler())]), af_cols),\n        ("cat", Pipeline([("imp", SimpleImputer(strategy="constant", fill_value="M")),\n                          ("oh", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown="ignore"))]), cat_cols),\n    ])\n\ny = tr_f["Survived"].values\nX = tr_f[num_cols + af_cols + cat_cols]\n\ndef fit_lr(Xf, yf):\n    p = Pipeline([("pre", make_pre()), ("lr", LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, random_state=SEED))]).fit(Xf, yf)\n    return p\ndef fit_et(Xf, yf, depth, leaf):\n    p = Pipeline([("pre", make_pre()), ("et", ExtraTreesClassifier(\n        n_estimators=400, max_depth=depth, min_samples_leaf=leaf,\n        random_state=SEED, n_jobs=4))]).fit(Xf, yf)\n    return p\n\nskf = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=SEED)\nfolds = list(skf.split(X, y))\nprint("folds:", [len(v) for _, v in folds])\n\ndef sweep(Xf):\n    rows = []\n    for depth in [5, 6, 7, 8]:\n        for leaf in [2, 3, 4, 6]:\n            oof_lr = np.zeros(len(y)); oof_et = np.zeros(len(y))\n            for tri, vai in folds:\n                lr = fit_lr(Xf.iloc[tri], y[tri])\n                et = fit_et(Xf.iloc[tri], y[tri], depth, leaf)\n                oof_lr[vai] = lr.predict_proba(Xf.iloc[vai])[:, 1]\n                oof_et[vai] = et.predict_proba(Xf.iloc[vai])[:, 1]\n            for w in [0.4, 0.5, 0.6, 0.7]:\n                prob = w * oof_lr + (1 - w) * oof_et\n                acc = accuracy_score(y, (prob >= 0.5).astype(int))\n                rows.append(dict(w=w, depth=depth, leaf=leaf, cv_acc=acc))\n    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n\nt0 = time.time()\nsweep_df = sweep(X)\nsweep_df = sweep_df.sort_values("cv_acc", ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\nsweep_df.to_csv(f"{WARD}/sweep_comparison.csv", index=False)\nprint("sweep time %.1fs, combos=%d" % (time.time() - t0, len(sweep_df)))\nprint(sweep_df.head(12).to_string())\n\n# also record incumbent CV for comparison\ndef cv_one(w, depth, leaf):\n    row = sweep_df[(sweep_df.w == w) & (sweep_df.depth == depth) & (sweep_df.leaf == leaf)]\n    return float(row["cv_acc"].values[0])\ninc_cv = cv_one(0.5, 6, 4)\nbest = sweep_df.iloc[0]\nprint("incumbent(0.5,6,4) CV=%.4f | best CV=%.4f (w=%.1f d=%d l=%d)" % (\n    inc_cv, best.cv_acc, best.w, best.depth, best.leaf))\n\n# ---- Final model: fit CV-chosen config on all 712 rows ----\nbw, bd, bl = float(best.w), int(best.depth), int(best.leaf)\nlr_final = fit_lr(X, y)\net_final = fit_et(X, y, bd, bl)\n\ndef blend_proba(lr, et, Xf, w):\n    return w * lr.predict_proba(Xf)[:, 1] + (1 - w) * et.predict_proba(Xf)[:, 1]\n\nXv = val_f[num_cols + af_cols + cat_cols]\nXt = te_f[num_cols + af_cols + cat_cols]\nval_pred = (blend_proba(lr_final, et_final, Xv, bw) >= 0.5).astype(int)\ntest_pred = (blend_proba(lr_final, et_final, Xt, bw) >= 0.5).astype(int)\n\npd.DataFrame({"PassengerId": val["PassengerId"], "Survived": val_pred}).to_csv(f"{WARD}/val_predictions.csv", index=False)\npp = pd.DataFrame({"PassengerId": test["PassengerId"], "Survived": test_pred})\npp.to_csv("predictions.csv", index=False)\n\nmetrics = {\n    "seed": SEED,\n    "cv_folds": 5,\n    "chosen": {"w": bw, "depth": bd, "leaf": bl, "cv_acc": float(best.cv_acc)},\n    "incumbent": {"w": 0.5, "depth": 6, "leaf": 4, "cv_acc": inc_cv, "fixed_val_accuracy": 0.8492},\n    "cv_gain": float(best.cv_acc - inc_cv),\n    "note": "prob>=0.5 -> 1; fixed-validation accuracy scored by evaluator; both val/test predictions from the same final model",\n}\njson.dump(metrics, open(f"{WARD}/metrics.json", "w"), indent=2)\njoblib.dump({"lr": lr_final, "et": et_final, "w": bw}, f"{WARD}/model_blend_best.joblib")\n\nopen(f"{WARD}/README.txt", "w").write(\n    "ROUND 4 - CV-tuned LR+ExtraTrees soft-vote\\n"\n    f"Chosen (5-fold CV on 712 rows): w={bw}, ET max_depth={bd}, min_samples_leaf={bl}, CV acc={best.cv_acc:.4f} "\n    f"(incumbent 0.5/6/4 CV={inc_cv:.4f})\\n"\n    "Inference: blend prob = w*p_LR + (1-w)*p_ET; Survived = 1 if prob>=0.5 else 0.\\n"\n    "Fit on all 712 train_data/train.csv rows; validation/test transform-only. Seed 42, CPU only.\\n"\n    "Deliverables: predictions.csv (418 rows), work/val_predictions.csv (179 rows) from the SAME model.\\n")\n\n# ---- assertions ----\nvp = pd.read_csv(f"{WARD}/val_predictions.csv")\nassert list(vp.columns) == ["PassengerId", "Survived"] and len(vp) == 179\nassert vp["PassengerId"].tolist() == val_ids\nassert list(pp.columns) == ["PassengerId", "Survived"] and len(pp) == 418\nassert pp["PassengerId"].tolist() == test["PassengerId"].tolist()\nassert set(vp["Survived"].unique()) <= {0, 1}\nassert set(pp["Survived"].unique()) <= {0, 1}\n\nprint("\\nFINAL: w=%.1f depth=%d leaf=%d | CV=%.4f vs incumbent CV=%.4f (val 0.8492)" % (\n    bw, bd, bl, best.cv_acc, inc_cv))\nprint("val pos rate %.3f | test pos rate %.3f" % (vp["Survived"].mean(), pp["Survived"].mean()))\nprint("wrote predictions.csv (418) and work/val_predictions.csv (179)")\n</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>work/val_predictions.csv</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>predictions.csv</prediction_file>'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Execution time: 14.98 seconds; success: True.\n<output>folds: [143, 143, 142, 142, 142]\nsweep time 13.7s, combos=64\n      w  depth  leaf    cv_acc\n0   0.4      6     3  0.830056\n1   0.4      5     2  0.828652\n2   0.4      7     6  0.828652\n3   0.4      8     6  0.828652\n4   0.4      5     3  0.828652\n5   0.4      6     6  0.828652\n6   0.4      5     4  0.828652\n7   0.7      8     2  0.827247\n8   0.4      5     6  0.827247\n9   0.4      6     4  0.827247\n10  0.4      8     4  0.827247\n11  0.7      8     3  0.825843\nincumbent(0.5,6,4) CV=0.8230 | best CV=0.8301 (w=0.4 d=6 l=3)\nFINAL: w=0.4 depth=6 leaf=3 | CV=0.8301 vs incumbent CV=0.8230 (val 0.8492)\nval pos rate 0.341 | test pos rate 0.383\nwrote predictions.csv (418) and work/val_predictions.csv (179)</output>\n<error></error>\nUse this evidence to repair failures or test the next controlled improvement.\n\nMeasured fixed-split validation metric: Metric↑(0.8436). Best so far: Metric↑(0.8436).\n\nRespond with exactly one executable notebook cell, using these tags:\n<goal>Hypothesis, expected runtime, expected output and how it tests the hypothesis</goal>\n<code>Python code for the next cell, without Markdown fences</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>Relative file path for complete validation predictions, or None</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>Relative file path for complete business prediction output, or None</prediction_file>\nBoth file tags must be None unless this cell writes BOTH complete outputs.\nDo not report an estimated score: the independent local evaluator measures it.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '<goal>RO