ll failed to beat 0.8492: round-4 CV-tuned blend (w=0.4, ET d=6/leaf=3) = 0.8436; interaction features (Sex_Pclass, FamilySize_bin) = 0.8212; LR+ET+GB 3-way vote = 0.8436; ET n_estimators 400->800 = 0.8436; decision threshold 0.45 = 0.8380; 5-seed bagging = 0.8436; CV-selected LR C=0.3 = 0.8380. ET criterion=\'entropy\' produced byte-identical predictions to gini (no change in metric). Each was reverted to the incumbent.\n\n**Changes from the parent.** The parent is the same LR+ExtraTrees soft-vote incumbent at w=0.5 with depth=6, leaf=4 (scored 0.8492). The best version is identical to the parent; all substantive changes attempted this round regressed, so the parent recipe was retained and re-verified.\n\n**Artifacts & loading (in `work/`):**\n- `work/model_blend_best.joblib`: dict with keys `lr`, `et` (full sklearn Pipelines including preprocessing), `w` (0.5), `n_estimators`, `threshold` (0.5), `lr_C` (1.0), `et_criterion` (\'gini\'). Load with `joblib.load("work/model_blend_best.joblib")`; predict via `w*lr.predict_proba(X)[:,1] + (1-w)*et.predict_proba(X)[:,1] >= threshold`, where `X` is the featurized DataFrame (FamilySize/IsAlone/Title/Embarked derived, raw columns selected).\n- `predictions.csv`: 418-row test predictions (PassengerId, Survived), original test order.\n- `work/val_predictions.csv`: 179-row validation predictions aligned to validation order.\n- `work/metrics.json`: config, metric 0.8492, full perturbation ledger, pinned md5s.\n- `work/README.txt`: inference instructions.\n\n**Reproducibility.** Seed 42, CPU, n_jobs=4, no downloads; val/test predictions come from the same single model and were asserted byte-identical to the pinned md5s on reload.\n</description>\n<code>\n# --- Best measured pipeline (canonical incumbent) ---\nimport joblib, numpy as np, pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, OneHotEncoder\nfrom sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import ExtraTreesClassifier\n\nSEED = 42\n# 1) load train/val/test (relative to ../input/data/)\n# 2) featurize: FamilySize, IsAlone, Title(rare<10->Rare via training counts), Embarked missing->\'M\'\n#    (same featurize applied to train/val/test; rare mapping computed from training Title counts only)\n# 3) shared ColumnTransformer:\n#      num[Pclass,SibSp,Parch,FamilySize,IsAlone] -> median impute + StandardScaler\n#      af [Age,Fare]                              -> median impute(add_indicator) + StandardScaler\n#      cat[Sex,Embarked,Title]                    -> constant \'M\' impute + OneHotEncoder(ignore)\n#    embedded in each Pipeline so preprocessing is fit inside the model pipeline on training rows only.\nlr = Pipeline([("pre", make_pre()), ("lr", LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, random_state=SEED))]).fit(X, y)\net = Pipeline([("pre", make_pre()), ("et", ExtraTreesClassifier(\n        n_estimators=400, max_depth=6, min_samples_leaf=4,\n        criterion="gini", random_state=SEED, n_jobs=4))]).fit(X, y)\n# 4) blend: prob = 0.5*lr.proba + 0.5*et.proba ; Survived = (prob >= 0.5)\n# 5) write predictions.csv (418) and work/val_predictions.csv (179) from this single model;\n#    persist joblib.dump({"lr","et","w":0.5,"threshold":0.5,...}, "work/model_blend_best.joblib")\n# 6) assert val/test PassengerId alignment, 0/1 domain, and reload-reproducibility.\n\n# Failed approach summary: 7 perturbations (CV blend tuning, interaction features, 3-way GB vote,\n# more trees, threshold 0.45, seed-bagging, LR C=0.3) each executed and regressed below 0.8492;\n# entropy criterion gave identical predictions. All were reverted to the incumbent.\n</code>\n<suggestions>\n**Observed weaknesses (evidence):**\n- The 179-row holdout is tiny; a single row is worth ~0.0056 accuracy, so perturbations move the score by only 1-4 rows and are dominated by noise. Round-4 and round-18 CV gains on 712 rows (+0.003 to +0.007 in 5-fold) failed to transfer to the holdout (both scored ~0.838-0.844) — CV-based selection is not a reliable proxy here.\n- Every added feature/model complexity (interactions, GradientBoosting, seed bagging, stronger ET) regressed; the incumbent is a stable optimum on this specific holdout.\n- Threshold and criterion changes either regressed (0.45) or were prediction-identical (entropy), implying the model\'s decision boundary is already saturated for these features.\n\n**Prioritized next experiments (hypotheses, not yet demonstrated):**\n1. Genuine new signal, not model tuning: the strongest untested Titanic predictor is likely `Cabin` deck (first letter), currently dropped. A fit-safe deck feature (missing -> \'U\') could add real information the current feature set lacks — test as a single controlled addition over the incumbent.\n2. Family/ticket-group survival features: shared `Ticket` prefix and group-size interactions sometimes carry signal; test one at a time and only keep if it beats 0.8492 on the fixed holdout (guard against the observed overfitting-on-179 pattern).\n3. If further tuning is pursued, consider that the evaluator\'s 712/179 split is the only reliable measuring stick — do not trust internal CV for final selection, since two CV-selected configs both regressed.\n4. Do NOT re-run already-rejected perturbations (interactions, GB, more trees, threshold shift, seed-bag, LR C, criterion) — they have executed negative evidence.\n\n**Lesson:** On this holdout the incumbent LR+ET (w=0.5, d=6, leaf=4) is the reproducible best; future rounds should either accept it as final or justify a *new-information* feature (e.g., Cabin deck) with a single controlled test rather than more hyperparameter search.\n</suggestions>', role='assistant', tool_calls=None, function_call=None, provider_specific_fields=None), provider_specific_fields={})], usage=Usage(completion_tokens=2031, prompt_tokens=55629, total_tokens=57660, completion_tokens_detai